e we got better information or the conditions that made them sensible changed. Longevity of a practice tells you it was adaptive to *something*, not that it's optimal now. So I'd separate two questions: does it feel unsettling to deviate from something that feels foundational? Probably, yes—that's a normal reaction to reconsidering inherited assumptions. Is that discomfort evidence that the traditional arrangement is actually correct for your specific family? Not really. What does your gut say when you strip away the "but this is how it's done" framing—do you have an actual preference for who goes back to work?
